<title>UK: Go-Ahead shares jump on rail bid hopes.</title>
<headline>Go-Ahead shares jump on rail bid hopes.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in UK transport company Go-Ahead Group Plc rose sharply on Thursday on speculation that its GOVIA joint venture would be announced as the preferred bidder for the Thameslink rail franchise.</p>
<p>The shares were up 25-1/2p at 502-1/2p by 1459 GMT.</p>
<p>Rail industry sources earlier told Reuters that GOVIA would shortly be named as the preferred bidder.</p>
</text>
